--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party binaries redistributed here
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

For the convenience of anyone fitting the gate without an Ada toolchain, this
repository ships two Free Software Foundation runtime libraries alongside our
own. They are NOT our work and are NOT under the AGPL:

  admission/lib/libgnat-15.dylib   GNAT run-time library
  admission/lib/libgcc_s.1.1.dylib GCC low-level run-time library

Both come from GNAT 15.0.1 20250418, Copyright (C) 1996-2025 Free Software
Foundation, Inc., built for arm64 macOS. They are licensed under the GNU
General Public License version 3 or later, WITH the GCC Runtime Library
Exception version 3.1 — which is what permits a program built with GNAT to be
distributed under a licence of its author's choosing.

WRITTEN OFFER OF SOURCE. The complete corresponding source for those two
libraries is the GCC source tree from which they were built, published by the
Free Software Foundation at https://gcc.gnu.org/ and mirrored by the FSF GNAT
packaging used to build them. If you would rather have it from us, write to
the address in the repository and we will send you a copy of that source, on
a medium customarily used for software interchange, for no more than our cost
of physically performing the distribution.

If you do not want third-party binaries in your supply chain — a defensible
position for a security library, and one we have sympathy with — delete
admission/lib/ entirely, install FSF GNAT yourself, and rebuild from source
with admission/build-lib.sh. admission/REPROVE.md walks the whole route,
including re-discharging the proofs. The digests in admission/DIGESTS.sha256
let you check that what you built matches what we shipped.
